==English==

==={{acronym}}===
'''TANSTAAFL'''

# {{idiom}} There [[ain't]] no such thing as a free lunch; something advertised as being "free" will invariably have hidden costs.

====Usage notes====
The most common form is emphatic, with ''[[ain't]],'' to convey a stronger jocular connotation than ''is.''  Compare to the milder [[TINSTAAFL]].

====Quotations====
*'''1966''', [[w:Robert Heinlein|Robert Heinlein]], ''[[w:The Moon Is A Harsh Mistress|The Moon Is A Harsh Mistress]]'',
*:"Gospodin," he said presently, "you used an odd word earlier--odd to me, I mean..."
*:"Oh, ''''tanstaafl'''.' Means 'There ain't no such thing as a free lunch.' And isn't," I added, pointing to a FREE LUNCH sign across room, "or these drinks would cost half as much. Was reminding her that anything free costs twice as much in long run or turns out worthless."
*'''1985''', [[w:Lance Parkin|Lance Parkin]], ''The Infinity Doctors'', page 229,
*:''''Tanstaafl'''.  There ain't no such thing as a free lunch. We both know that I was brought here for a reason.  If we could get down to business.'
*'''2009''', [[Dr. Elefun]], ''[[Astro Boy (Film)]]
*The Doctor unveils the pure positive energy of the the Blue Core and says, "Unfortunately, there's no such thing as a free lunch," referring to the pure negative energy left after the Blue Core's extraction, known as the Red Core.
